Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:37:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Input: aw8695 - add firmware-free AW8697 finite-burst
 support

[V] Port Luca Weiss's GPL-2.0-only driver from the public SM8250 tree,
tag 7.2.0-dev. Preserve copyright. Generate a sine period at the
configured resonance using Linux fixed-point arithmetic. The imported
fixed period was about 235 Hz at 24 kHz, mismatching this actuator's
170 Hz. No vendor waveform firmware is requested.

Validate parameters before arithmetic, propagate missing trace
properties, and request IRQs after initialization. Clean up work and
reset at removal or probe failure. Bound playback in hardware, scale
gain by magnitude, latch protection faults into reset, and stop at
close, suspend and shutdown.

Probe performs bounded resonance calibration. Board nodes stay
disabled. [I] Hardware operation remains untested. No maintainer has
accepted this bring-up driver; list files as odd fixes without
assigning a person.

Source:

https://gitlab.nura.eco/soc/qualcomm-sm8250/linux/-/blob/3c5440e9dd3c3e3b5735ad8f1b22bdfd02c707d9/drivers/input/misc/aw8695-haptics.c

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
